it's only implied; it says that it's safe to pray "unless you have some
reason to believe that your luck is still bad even after this luck
increase".  Neither pray.txt nor gems-343.txt indicate how much of a
luck increase four-leaf clovers give; my best guess is that it falls
under this line in gems-343.txt:

   0 to +5  Sacrificing, god happy.

The reason I'm bringing this up is that my wizard found the luckstone
at Mine's End (it's been positively ID'd now), and I've had several
rounds of sac-festing, including one which got me crowned, and yet I
keep seeing four-leaf clovers.  I was under the impression that it only
took a few clovers to max out luck, and I haven't done anything to
decrease my luck that I'm aware of (no broken mirrors, etc.)  I had an
uncursed luckstone in my main inventory before the first sac-fest; it's
never been dropped/cursed/stashed, though I did just bless it.

Is it possible to see a clover, even if your luck is already maxed out?
 How much does seeing a clover actually affect your luck, anyhow?

